<title>USA: Greyhound finances 209 buses for $53 million.</title>
<headline>Greyhound finances 209 buses for $53 million.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Greyhound Lines Inc said it financed 209 new inner-city buses for $53 million.</p>
<p>The financings were structured as single investor leases, Greyhound said. They were placed with seven financial institutions, including BancBoston Leasing Inc, and Carlson Leasing Inc, among others, the company added.</p>
<p>The company was not immediately available to comment further.</p>
</text>
